r><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">490209</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><label>14</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Zello</surname><given-names>G.A.</given-names></name><name><surname>Pencharz</surname><given-names>P.B.</given-names></name><name><surname>Ball</surname><given-names>R.O.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Dietary lysine requirement of young adult males determined by oxidation of L-[1-13C] phenylalanine</article-title><source>Am. J. Physiol.</source><volume>264</volume><fpage>E677</fpage><lpage>685</lpage><year>1993</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8476044</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><label>15</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hsu</surname><given-names>J.W.</given-names></name><name><surname>Goonewardene</surname><given-names>L.A.</given-names></name><name><surname>Rafii</surname><given-names>M.</given-names></name><name><surname>Ball</surname><given-names>R.O.</given-names></name><name><surname>Pencharz</surname><given-names>P.B.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Aromatic amino acid requirements in healthy men measured by indicator amino acid oxidation</article-title><source>Am. J. Clin. Nutr.</source><volume>83</volume><fpage>82</fpage><lpage>88</lpage><year>2006</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16400054</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><label>16</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Robbins</surname><given-names>K.R.</given-names></name><name><surname>Saxton</surname><given-names>A.M.</given-names></name><name><surname>Southern</surname><given-names>L.L.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Estimation of nutrient requirements using broken-line regression analysis</article-title><source>J. Anim. Sci.</source><volume>84</volume><fpage>E155</fpage><lpage>165</lpage><year>2006</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16582088</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><label>17</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hudson</surname><given-names>D.J.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Fitting segmented curves whose join points have to be estimated</article-title><source>J. Amer. Statist. Assoc.</source><volume> 61</volume><fpage>1097</fpage><lpage>1129</lpage><year>1966</year></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><label>18</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hastie</surname><given-names>T.</given-names></name><name><surname>Tibshirani</surname><given-names>R.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Varying-coefficient models</article-title><source>J. Royal Statist. Soc. B. Stat. Methodol.</source><volume>55</volume><fpage>757</fpage><lpage>796</lpage><year>1993</year></citation></ref></ref-list></back><floats-wrap><fig id="F1" position="float"><label>Fig.&#x000a0;1</label><caption><p>Fitted regression lines for three models. Each panel shows measurements of subjects in the placebo (open circle) and the experimental groups (closed circle) with regression lines for the placebo (dashed line) and experimental groups (solid line). Regression lines in Panel A are by the Change-point regression model (Eq 1), those in Panel B are by ANCOVA (Eq 2) and those in Panel C are by ANCOVA with interaction (Eq 3).</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="jcbn08-245f01"/></fig><fig id="F2" position="float"><label>Fig.&#x000a0;2</label><caption><p>Result of Change-point regression model (CPRM) for Garcinia study (combined data). The open and closed circles mean placebo and treatment groups, respectively. Panel A is profile of AICs of CPRM with a change point of <italic>x</italic><sub><italic>cp</italic></sub>: minimum AIC is attained at <italic>x</italic><sub><italic>cp</italic></sub> is 62.4 (cm<sup>2</sup>). Panel B is Scatter plot of VFA at the study end versus Pre-VFA with regression lines for placebo (dashed line) and experimental groups (solid line) by CPRM with a change-point of 62.4&#x000a0;cm<sup>2</sup> in Garcinia study: the treatment group was effective only for subjects with Pre-VFA greater than 62.4&#x000a0;cm<sup>2</sup>.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="jcbn08-245f02"/></fig><fig id="F3" position="float"><label>Fig.&#x000a0;3</label><caption><p>Result of Change-point regression model (CPRM) for Garcinia study. Panel A is profile of AICs of CPRM with a change-point of <italic>x</italic><sub><italic>cp</italic></sub>: minimum AIC is attained at <italic>x</italic><sub><italic>cp</italic></sub> and is 68.7 (cm<sup>2</sup>). Panel B is Scatter plot of VFA at the study end versus Pre-VFA with regression lines for placebo (dashed line) and experimental groups (solid line) by CPRM with a change-point of 68.7&#x000a0;cm<sup>2</sup> for Garcinia study: the treatment group is effective only for subjects with Pre-VFA greater than 68.7&#x000a0;cm<sup>2</sup>.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="jcbn08-245f03"/></fig><table-wrap id="T1" position="float"><label>Table&#x000a0;1</label><caption><p>Summary of Garcinia studies</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><th rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><th align="center" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Study design</th><th align="center" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Subject diagnosis</th><th align="center" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Number of subject</th><th align="center" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Dosage in mg/day (duration)</th><th align="center" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">VFA at baseline (range) (cm<sup>2</sup>)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Study 1</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Randomized, placebo-controlled, double-blind</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Overweight</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">40 (20 male, 20 female)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1000&#x000a0;mg (&#x02212;)-HCA (8 weeks)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">83.0 (26.2&#x02013;143.0)</td></tr><tr><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Study 2</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Randomized, placebo-controlled, double-blind</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Overweight or obese</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">39 (18 male, 21 female)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1000&#x000a0;mg (&#x02212;)-HCA (12 weeks)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">145.5 (90.4&#x02013;244.3)</td></tr></tbody></table></table-wrap><table-wrap id="T2" position="float"><label>Table&#x000a0;2</label><caption><p>AIC of CPRM and ANCOVA models for Gracinia study</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Model</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">AIC</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">CPRM with <italic>x</italic><sub><italic>cp</italic></sub> of 62.4 (Eq 1)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">667.184</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">ANCOVA (Eq 2)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">685.930</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">ANCOVA with interaction (Eq 3)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">667.605</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">T-test (Eq 4)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">684.969</td></tr></tbody></table></table-wrap><table-wrap id="T3" position="float"><label>Table&#x000a0;3</label><caption><p>ANOVA table of CPRM with <italic>x</italic><sub><italic>cp</italic></sub> of 62.4 in Garcinia study</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><th rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Estimate Coefficient</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">SE</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><italic>t</italic> value</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><italic>p</italic> value</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x003b2;<sub>0</sub></td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02212;6.884</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">4.827</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02212;1.426</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.158</td></tr><tr><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x003b2;<sub>1</sub></td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1.105</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.044</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">25.032</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x0003c;0.0001</td></tr><tr><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x003b2;<sub>2</sub></td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02212;0.322</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.051</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02212;6.262</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x0003c;0.0001</td></tr></tbody></table></table-wrap></floats-wrap></article>